## Paper Table 3 (C0) `tables/t1_mechanisms.tex` (appendix companion, paper Table 4: `tables/t1_calibration_full.tex`, all s)
`booktabs` tabular, 383 pt wide at `\small`; put it in a `table` with `\small` and `\centering`. Caption draft: **The six interference mechanisms and their calibration at the core cell (s = 0.5, sigma = 0.5).**
z_i own treatment, f_i treated-neighbour fraction, c_i treated-neighbour count, d-bar mean degree, W the row-normalised adjacency matrix. Every mechanism is calibrated to the GATE tau = 1 (exact value 0.9999 to 1.0000 over all columns; (e) is 0.99987 at s = 0.75 because of the 30-step truncation) and to the spillover share s (direct effect 1 - s).
DM bias: measured mean normalised DM error; SNR: variance of the treatment part of the outcome over the noise variance; noise share: share of the Chin regression's variance that is outcome noise (exact). With a correct specification and sigma = 0 the error is below 5e-9 (`tables/t1_mechanisms_caption_facts.txt`).

